### Geocoding Service API Examples
###
### Endpoints
###   GET  /features      – which optional features are enabled
###   GET  /health        – dependency health check (ES, PostGIS, NATS, Redis, Ollama)
###   GET  /autocomplete  – fast prefix-based suggestions (Redis sorted sets, ~1-3ms)
###   GET  /geocode       – full-text + vector + geo search (with address interpolation fallback)
###   GET  /address       – structured address search (with address interpolation fallback)
###   GET  /reverse       – reverse geocoding (lat/lon → nearest address / interpolated / street / boundaries)
###   GET  /deep/forward  – deep forward geocoding via Google Maps (maps→OSM tags, publishes to NATS, geocode-shaped)
###   GET  /deep/reverse  – deep reverse geocoding via Google Maps (maps→OSM tags, publishes to NATS, reverse-shaped)
###   GET  /deep/nearby   – deep nearby search via Google Places (maps→OSM tags, publishes to NATS, nearby-shaped)
###   GET  /describe      – AI-generated title + description for a place
###   POST /feedback      – popularity feedback loop
###   POST /places        – add a custom place
###   POST /insert        – insert raw OSM element via NATS
###   POST /traffic/probe  – submit one GPS ping for live-traffic aggregation
###   POST /traffic/probes – submit a GPS trace (batch) for live-traffic aggregation
###   GET  /traffic/edge   – current live speed for the road edge nearest a point
###   GET  /nearby         – explore nearby places, filter by category/group, with distance_m
###   GET  /nearby/categories – list the filterable groups and their category values
###
### Routing (Valhalla, on {{routeUrl}} — host port 8001):
###   GET  /status            – engine/tileset status & loaded actions
###   POST /route             – turn-by-turn directions (multi-stop supported)
###   POST /optimized_route   – reorders stops for the shortest tour (TSP)
###   POST /sources_to_targets – time/distance matrix (many → many)
###   POST /isochrone         – reachability polygons (e.g. 10/20 min by car)
###   POST /locate            – snap input coords to the road network
###
### Shared query flags for the search endpoints:
###   vector=true|false   – enable/disable semantic vector re-ranking
###   ai=true|false       – enable/disable AI-assisted expansion
###   describe=true|false – include AI-generated title + description (cached)

@baseUrl = http://84.8.102.106:8000
#@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

# Valhalla routing engine (turn-by-turn directions, matrices, isochrones).
@routeUrl = http://84.8.102.106:8001
#@routeUrl = http://localhost:8001
#
# ============================================================================
# /features  –  Feature flags
# ============================================================================

### Report which optional features (vectors, AI) are enabled on this instance
GET {{baseUrl}}/features

###

# ============================================================================
# /health  –  Dependency health check
# ============================================================================

### Check all backend dependencies: ES, PostGIS, NATS, Redis, Ollama.
### Returns 200 (healthy) or 503 (degraded) with per-service status.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

###

# ============================================================================
# /autocomplete  –  Fast prefix-based suggestions (Redis sorted sets)
#
# Designed for keystroke-by-keystroke dropdown suggestions. The primary path
# is a Redis sorted-set lookup (~1-3 ms); if Redis is unavailable it falls
# back to an Elasticsearch edge-ngram query. The response carries a
# "source": "redis"|"elasticsearch" field so you can see which path served it.
#
# Params:
#   q       (required) – partial query text (min 1 char)
#   lat/lon            – geo-bias: prefer results near this location
#   limit              – max suggestions (1–20, default 7)
# ============================================================================

### First few characters
GET {{baseUrl}}/autocomplete?q=cai

###

### Longer prefix narrows the suggestions
GET {{baseUrl}}/autocomplete?q=cairo

###

### Arabic prefix
GET {{baseUrl}}/autocomplete?q=القاه

###

### Street-name prefix
GET {{baseUrl}}/autocomplete?q=tahrir

###

### Geo-biased – prefer suggestions near downtown Cairo
GET {{baseUrl}}/autocomplete?q=corn&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357

###

### Address-like prefix (street + city)
GET {{baseUrl}}/autocomplete?q=tahrir street cai&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357

###

### Short prefix with geo-bias, raised limit (nearby restaurants)
GET {{baseUrl}}/autocomplete?q=rest&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10

###

### Single character (minimum allowed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/autocomplete?q=a&limit=5

###

# ============================================================================
# /describe  –  AI-generated title + description for a place
#
# Returns a bilingual (Arabic + English) title and description. The first call
# blocks until generation completes, then the result is cached. Requires
# Ollama to be running with the configured model.
#
# Params:
#   osm_id  (required) – OSM ID of the place to describe
# ============================================================================

### Describe a node (blocks until ready on first call)
GET {{baseUrl}}/describe?osm_id=n271613766

###

### Describe a way
GET {{baseUrl}}/describe?osm_id=w888001

###

# ============================================================================
# /geocode  –  Full-text + vector + geo-decay search
#
# Params:
#   q       (required) – free-text query
#   lat/lon            – bias results toward this location
#   limit              – max results per page (1–50, default 10)
#   offset             – result offset for paging/scrolling (0–9950, default 0;
#                        offset + limit must stay ≤ 10000)
#   vector=true|false  – enable/disable semantic vector re-ranking
#   ai=true|false      – enable/disable AI-assisted expansion
#   describe=true|false – include AI descriptions (cached where available)
#   effort=high|optimized – scoring effort (default high). 'high' = full fuzzy
#                        recall + per-doc function_score over all matches.
#                        'optimized' = lean fuzzy + function_score applied via
#                        rescore over the top hits only + track_total_hits off;
#                        far cheaper for ES under load (use when geocode traffic
#                        is stalling Elasticsearch). In optimized mode
#                        pagination.total is null.
#
# The response carries a `pagination` block: { limit, offset, total, has_more }.
# To scroll, re-request with offset += limit until has_more is false.
# ============================================================================

### Basic name search
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=makaram

###

### Geo-biased search near the Giza Pyramids
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=pyramids&lat=29.9792&lon=31.1342&limit=5

###

### Multi-word search with Cairo location bias
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=tahrir square&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10

###

### Text-only search, vector re-ranking disabled (faster)
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=alexandria&limit=10&vector=false

###

### Fuzzy / typo-tolerant search (Latin typo of an English name)
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=alexandira&lat=31.2001&lon=29.9187&limit=5

###

### Cross-script romanization — NOTE: "kahira" (romanized القاهرة) does NOT
### currently return the city Cairo. Cairo's name_en is the exonym "Cairo"
### and its name is Arabic script, so a Latin romanization has nothing to
### match except buried alt-names in tags_text. Needs a transliteration /
### dedicated alt-name field to work (see backlog).
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=kahira&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=5

###

### Venue-type search near Cairo
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=restaurant&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=15

###

### Address-like query: housenumber + street clauses are added automatically
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=10 Tahrir Street, Cairo&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=5

###

### Arabic name search
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=القاهرة&limit=10

###

### Include AI descriptions (cached where available, null otherwise)
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=cairo tower&lat=30.0459&lon=31.2243&limit=5&describe=true

###

### Address interpolation – housenumber that may not exist in the DB.
### If "15 Tahrir Street" is missing, its position is interpolated from nearby
### addresses (e.g. #10 and #20). The interpolated result appears first with
### match_type "interpolated", a side ("odd"/"even"), and bracket_low/high.
###
### Cross-language: the street name is resolved through Elasticsearch first, so an
### English query ("Tahrir Street") reaches the Arabic-tagged address points on
### شارع التحرير. lat/lon disambiguates between same-named streets across the city
### (many شارع التحرير in Cairo) by snapping to the nearest cluster.
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=15 Tahrir Street, Cairo&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=5

###

### Odd/even detection – addresses are split by street side (parity) and
### interpolated along the correct side.
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=22 Kasr El Aini Street, Cairo&lat=30.0380&lon=31.2336&limit=5

###

### Scroll / paginate – page 1 (first 10). Check pagination.has_more in the response.
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=makaram&limit=10&offset=0

###

### Scroll / paginate – page 2 (next 10). Re-request with offset += limit.
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=makaram&limit=10&offset=10

###

### Effort: high (default) – full fuzzy recall, function_score over all matches.
### features.effort echoes the mode; pagination.total carries the exact count.
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=tahrir square&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10&effort=high

###

### Effort: optimized – lean fuzzy + rescore over top hits, no exact counting.
### Much lighter on ES under load. Same top results in the common case;
### pagination.total is null (exact counting disabled). Compare against the
### high-effort request above to see the ranking is unchanged for typical queries.
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=tahrir square&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10&effort=optimized

###

### Optimized effort on a typo query – fuzzy still resolves the near-exact match,
### just with a tighter automaton (prefix_length 2, capped expansions).
GET {{baseUrl}}/geocode?q=alexandira&lat=31.2001&lon=29.9187&limit=5&effort=optimized

###

# ============================================================================
# /address  –  Structured address search
#
# Params:
#   q        (required) – free-form or structured address string
#   lat/lon             – proximity boost (tight 1 km decay)
#   limit               – max results (1–50, default 10)
#   postcode            – hard filter: restrict to this postal code
#   city                – hard filter: restrict to this city
#   country             – hard filter: restrict to ISO country code (e.g. EG)
#   describe=true|false – include AI descriptions (cached where available)
#
# The response includes a `parsed` field showing how the query was decomposed.
# ============================================================================

### Full address: housenumber + street + city (auto-parsed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=10 Tahrir Street, Cairo

###

### Street and city, no house number
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=Tahrir Street, Cairo&limit=10

###

### Street with city supplied as an explicit filter param
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=Corniche El Nil&city=Cairo&limit=10

###

### Street with country restriction
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=Nile Street&country=EG&limit=10

###

### Postcode lookup – all addresses in a postal district
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=11511

###

### Postcode as a hard filter combined with a street query
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=Tahrir Street&postcode=11511

###

### Proximity bias near Tahrir Square
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=Tahrir Street&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10

###

### Housenumber + street + city, with proximity and country filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=15 Kasr El Aini Street, Cairo&lat=30.0380&lon=31.2336&country=EG&limit=5

###

### Arabic address – street in Arabic script
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=شارع التحرير, القاهرة

###

### Arabic full address with housenumber and proximity
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=10 شارع التحرير, القاهرة&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357

###

### Suburb / neighbourhood search
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=Zamalek, Cairo&lat=30.0614&lon=31.2208&limit=10

###

### Alexandria address with proximity
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=Corniche Road, Alexandria&lat=31.2088&lon=29.9183&limit=10

###

### Minimal – single street name, capped to 5 results
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=El Galaa Street&limit=5

###

### Address search with AI descriptions
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=10 Tahrir Street, Cairo&describe=true

###

### Address interpolation – same odd/even fallback as /geocode
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=17 Corniche El Nil&city=Cairo&limit=5

###

### Interpolation with country filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/address?q=33 El Galaa Street&country=EG&limit=5

###

# ============================================================================
# /reverse  –  Reverse geocoding (PostGIS + Elasticsearch)
#
# Params:
#   lat  (required) – latitude
#   lon  (required) – longitude
#   describe=true|false – include AI descriptions on nearest_line / polygons
#
# Returns:
#   nearest_address      – closest building/address point (housenumber, street,
#                          city, postcode, country, full_address, distance_m, …)
#   interpolated_address – estimated address at the query point, interpolated
#                          from nearby same-street addresses with odd/even
#                          detection; null if fewer than 2 addresses nearby
#   nearest_line         – closest road/path (LineString) with ES metadata
#   enclosing_polygons   – all polygons containing the point (admin boundaries,
#                          landuse, …) sorted by admin_level (most specific first)
# ============================================================================

### Tahrir Square, Cairo
GET {{baseUrl}}/reverse?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357

###

### Near the Giza Pyramids
GET {{baseUrl}}/reverse?lat=29.9792&lon=31.1342

###

### Downtown Alexandria
GET {{baseUrl}}/reverse?lat=31.2088&lon=29.9183

###

### Zamalek (Cairo island district)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reverse?lat=30.0614&lon=31.2208

###

### Near the Nile in Cairo
GET {{baseUrl}}/reverse?lat=30.0500&lon=31.2336

###

### Heliopolis (northeast Cairo)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reverse?lat=30.0928&lon=31.3201

###

### Aswan (southern Egypt)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reverse?lat=24.0889&lon=32.8998

###

### With AI descriptions on streets/polygons
GET {{baseUrl}}/reverse?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&describe=true

###

# ============================================================================
# /deep/forward  &  /deep/reverse  –  Deep geocoding via Google Maps
#
# These call the Google Maps Geocoding API, MAP each result into OSM tags
# (addr:* + feature tags like amenity/shop/tourism + name + source=google),
# PUBLISH the mapped element to NATS so the inserters index it, then RETURN the
# data enriched and shaped exactly like /geocode and /reverse.
#
# Requires GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY to be set (and ENABLE_DEEP=true). Without a key
# the endpoints return 503. The response adds "source":"google" and
# "published": <count of elements pushed to NATS for indexing>.
#
# The same place requested in different languages maps to the SAME document
# (osm_id is a hash of the Google place_id); the indexer MERGES the names so the
# doc accumulates name:en / name:ar / … like a multilingual OSM element.
#
# /deep/forward params:
#   q        (required) – free-text place/address query
#   language (required) – result language: en, ar, fr, …
#   limit               – max results (1–25, default 10)
#   region              – ccTLD region bias, e.g. eg
#   publish=true|false  – publish mapped results to NATS (default true)
#   enrich=true|false   – attach parent/nearest-street enrichment (default true)
#
# /deep/reverse params:
#   lat, lon (required) – coordinates to resolve
#   language (required) – result language: en, ar, fr, …
#   publish=true|false  – publish mapped results to NATS (default true)
#   describe=true|false – AI descriptions on local geometry context
# ============================================================================

### Deep forward (English) – resolve a place via Google, index it, return geocode-shaped
GET {{baseUrl}}/deep/forward?q=Cairo Tower&language=en&region=eg&limit=5

###

### Deep forward (Arabic) – SAME place, different language → merged onto the same doc
GET {{baseUrl}}/deep/forward?q=Cairo Tower&language=ar&region=eg&limit=5

###

### Deep forward without publishing (just resolve + return, don't index)
GET {{baseUrl}}/deep/forward?q=15 Tahrir Street, Cairo&language=en&publish=false

###

### Deep reverse – resolve an address for a point via Google, index it, return reverse-shaped
GET {{baseUrl}}/deep/reverse?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&language=en

###

# ============================================================================
# /deep/nearby  –  Deep nearby search via Google Places API (New) Text Search
#   Maps each place → OSM tags, publishes to NATS for indexing, returns
#   nearby-shaped rows (distance_m + category).
#   lat/lon/language + (type OR keyword) required · radius = location bias
#   rankby=prominence|distance · limit ≤20/page · cursor (scroll) · publish
#   Scroll: pass a response's pagination.next_cursor back as cursor.
#   Needs GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY + ENABLE_DEEP + "Places API (New)" on the project.
# ============================================================================

### Nearby restaurants, relevance-ranked, indexed + returned
GET {{baseUrl}}/deep/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=1000&type=restaurant&language=en

###

### Nearest-first cafes (rankby=distance)
GET {{baseUrl}}/deep/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&type=cafe&rankby=distance&language=en

###

### Keyword search (Arabic names), preview only without indexing
GET {{baseUrl}}/deep/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=2000&keyword=صيدلية&language=ar&publish=false

###

### Scroll page 1 — take pagination.next_cursor from the response.
GET {{baseUrl}}/deep/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=1500&type=restaurant&language=en&limit=20

###

### Scroll page 2 — replace <CURSOR> with next_cursor (keep other params identical).
GET {{baseUrl}}/deep/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=1500&type=restaurant&language=en&limit=20&cursor=<CURSOR>

###

# ============================================================================
# /feedback  –  Popularity feedback loop
#
# Increments the popularity field for an osm_id (in ES and Redis). Higher
# popularity raises the element's ranking in future /geocode results.
#
# Params:
#   osm_id  (required) – OSM ID to boost
#   boost              – increment, clamped to [0.1, 10.0] (default 1.0)
# ============================================================================

### Default boost (+1.0)
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback?osm_id=n271613766&boost=1.0

###

### Stronger boost for a frequently-clicked result
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback?osm_id=n271613766&boost=5.0

###

# ============================================================================
# /places  –  Add a custom place
#
# Publishes to the NATS stream; picked up by es-inserter and postgis-inserter.
# Address fields: addr_housenumber, addr_street, addr_city, addr_postcode,
#                 addr_country, addr_suburb, addr_state.
# ============================================================================

### Minimal – name + coordinates
POST {{baseUrl}}/places
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Downtown Cafe",
  "lat": 30.0500,
  "lon": 31.2400,
  "tags": { "amenity": "cafe" }
}

###

### Restaurant with address fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/places
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nile View Restaurant",
  "name_en": "Nile View Restaurant",
  "lat": 30.0444,
  "lon": 31.2357,
  "osm_type": "node",
  "admin_level": 8,
  "tags": {
    "amenity": "restaurant",
    "cuisine": "egyptian"
  },
  "addr_housenumber": "5",
  "addr_street": "Corniche El Nil",
  "addr_city": "Cairo",
  "addr_postcode": "11511",
  "addr_country": "EG"
}

###

### Building with a full address (appears in /address and /reverse results)
POST {{baseUrl}}/places
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Office Tower",
  "lat": 30.0380,
  "lon": 31.2336,
  "osm_type": "node",
  "tags": { "building": "commercial" },
  "addr_housenumber": "22",
  "addr_street": "Kasr El Aini Street",
  "addr_suburb": "Garden City",
  "addr_city": "Cairo",
  "addr_postcode": "11516",
  "addr_country": "EG"
}

###

### Museum with English name and tags
POST {{baseUrl}}/places
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "متحف مصر",
  "name_en": "Egyptian Museum",
  "lat": 30.0479,
  "lon": 31.2355,
  "osm_type": "node",
  "admin_level": 8,
  "tags": {
    "tourism": "museum",
    "historic": "yes"
  },
  "addr_street": "El Tahrir Square",
  "addr_city": "Cairo",
  "addr_country": "EG"
}

###

# ============================================================================
# /insert  –  Raw OSM element insertion (matches watcher.py message format)
#
# Useful for injecting test data or replaying elements.
# ============================================================================

### Node with address tags (indexed as an address point)
POST {{baseUrl}}/insert
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "osm_id": "n999001",
  "osm_type": "node",
  "tags": {
    "name": "Sample Building",
    "building": "yes",
    "addr:housenumber": "42",
    "addr:street": "Tahrir Street",
    "addr:city": "Cairo",
    "addr:postcode": "11511",
    "addr:country": "EG"
  },
  "geom": {
    "type": "Point",
    "coordinates": [31.2357, 30.0444]
  },
  "admin_level": 0,
  "area_km2": 0.0
}

###

### Way (road/LineString) – becomes a nearest_line candidate in /reverse
POST {{baseUrl}}/insert
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "osm_id": "w888001",
  "osm_type": "way",
  "tags": {
    "name": "Tahrir Street",
    "name:en": "Tahrir Street",
    "highway": "primary",
    "addr:street": "Tahrir Street"
  },
  "geom": {
    "type": "LineString",
    "coordinates": [
      [31.2340, 30.0440],
      [31.2355, 30.0444],
      [31.2370, 30.0448]
    ]
  },
  "admin_level": 0,
  "area_km2": 0.0
}

###

### Administrative boundary polygon – becomes an enclosing_polygon in /reverse
POST {{baseUrl}}/insert
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "osm_id": "r777001",
  "osm_type": "relation",
  "tags": {
    "name": "Cairo Governorate",
    "name:en": "Cairo Governorate",
    "boundary": "administrative",
    "admin_level": "4"
  },
  "geom": {
    "type": "Polygon",
    "coordinates": [[
      [31.1, 29.9],
      [31.5, 29.9],
      [31.5, 30.2],
      [31.1, 30.2],
      [31.1, 29.9]
    ]]
  },
  "admin_level": 4,
  "area_km2": 3085.0
}

###

# ============================================================================
# ROUTING  –  Valhalla routing engine  ({{routeUrl}}, host port 8001)
#
# Valhalla is built from data/egypt-latest.osm.pbf at first container start
# (the graph build can take several minutes — watch `docker compose logs -f
# valhalla` and wait for /status to return 200 before sending route requests).
#
# All routing requests are POSTs with a JSON body. Coordinates are {lat, lon}.
# `costing` selects the travel profile: auto | bicycle | pedestrian | bus |
# truck | motor_scooter | taxi. See https://valhalla.github.io/valhalla/api/
# ============================================================================

### Status – engine version, loaded tileset bbox, available actions.
### Use this to confirm the graph finished building before routing.
GET {{routeUrl}}/status

###

### Driving directions – Cairo (Tahrir Sq.) → Alexandria, turn-by-turn.
### `narrative` maneuvers + total time/distance come back under trip.legs.
POST {{routeUrl}}/route
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "type": "break" },
    { "lat": 31.2001, "lon": 29.9187, "type": "break" }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers", "language": "en-US" }
}

###

### Driving directions in Arabic narrative (language=ar) – Tahrir → Giza Pyramids
POST {{routeUrl}}/route
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers", "language": "ar-SA" }
}

###

### Multi-destination route (several stops in order) – a single trip that
### visits Tahrir → Zamalek → Heliopolis → Giza Pyramids. Intermediate stops
### are "through" points (no stop) here; use "break" to force a stop/leg split.
POST {{routeUrl}}/route
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "type": "break" },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208, "type": "through" },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201, "type": "through" },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342, "type": "break" }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

###

### Optimized route (TSP) – same stops, but Valhalla reorders the middle
### waypoints to minimise total drive time. First & last locations are fixed.
POST {{routeUrl}}/optimized_route
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

###

### Time/distance matrix (multi-destination) – drive time & distance from one
### origin (Tahrir) to several destinations at once. Response: sources_to_targets
### with `time` (s) and `distance` (km/mi) for each source→target pair.
POST {{routeUrl}}/sources_to_targets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sources": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 }
  ],
  "targets": [
    { "lat": 31.2001, "lon": 29.9187 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201 },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "units": "kilometers"
}

###

### Full many-to-many matrix – every origin to every destination (e.g. for a
### fleet/dispatch grid). Here 3 sources × 3 targets = 9 cost cells.
POST {{routeUrl}}/sources_to_targets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sources": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208 },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201 }
  ],
  "targets": [
    { "lat": 30.0479, "lon": 31.2355 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 },
    { "lat": 31.2001, "lon": 29.9187 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "units": "kilometers"
}

