###

### Isochrone – how far can you drive from Tahrir Sq. in 10 / 20 / 30 minutes?
### Returns GeoJSON reachability polygons (one per contour).
POST {{routeUrl}}/isochrone
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "contours": [
    { "time": 10, "color": "ff0000" },
    { "time": 20, "color": "00ff00" },
    { "time": 30, "color": "0000ff" }
  ],
  "polygons": true
}

###

### Locate – snap raw coordinates onto the routing graph (nearest edges/nodes).
### Useful for debugging "why won't this point route?" and verbose edge info.
POST {{routeUrl}}/locate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "verbose": true
}

###

# ============================================================================
# LIVE TRAFFIC  –  crowdsourced GPS probes feeding Valhalla
#
# App users stream GPS pings to the geocoder ({{baseUrl}}, requires
# ENABLE_TRAFFIC=true). The traffic-aggregator map-matches them to Valhalla
# edges and keeps a smoothed per-edge speed in Redis; the traffic-writer pushes
# those speeds into Valhalla's traffic.tar. Routes then bend around congestion
# when they ask for live traffic (date_time.type=0 + speed_types incl. "current").
#
# A probe ping: { lat, lon, speed?(m/s), heading?(deg), ts?(epoch seconds) }.
# A batch (ordered trace from one device) map-matches far better than single
# points, so prefer /traffic/probes with several points.
# ============================================================================

### Submit a GPS trace of SLOW pings (~3 m/s ≈ 11 km/h) along Tahrir → Giza.
### Send this a few times (>= TRAFFIC_MIN_SAMPLES) to mark these edges congested.
POST {{baseUrl}}/traffic/probes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "device_id": "demo-device-1",
  "points": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "speed": 3.0, "ts": 1750000000 },
    { "lat": 30.0429, "lon": 31.2300, "speed": 2.5, "ts": 1750000020 },
    { "lat": 30.0410, "lon": 31.2230, "speed": 3.2, "ts": 1750000045 },
    { "lat": 30.0388, "lon": 31.2150, "speed": 2.8, "ts": 1750000075 },
    { "lat": 30.0360, "lon": 31.2050, "speed": 3.0, "ts": 1750000110 }
  ]
}

###

### Submit a free-flow trace (~25 m/s ≈ 90 km/h) — useful to clear congestion.
POST {{baseUrl}}/traffic/probes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "device_id": "demo-device-2",
  "points": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "speed": 25.0, "ts": 1750000000 },
    { "lat": 30.0429, "lon": 31.2300, "speed": 24.0, "ts": 1750000003 },
    { "lat": 30.0410, "lon": 31.2230, "speed": 26.0, "ts": 1750000006 },
    { "lat": 30.0388, "lon": 31.2150, "speed": 25.5, "ts": 1750000010 }
  ]
}

###

### Submit a single GPS ping (device_id is a query param here).
POST {{baseUrl}}/traffic/probe?device_id=demo-device-3
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "speed": 4.0, "ts": 1750000000 }

###

### Inspect the current live speed for the edge nearest a point (debug/ops).
### Returns the snapped edge_id (Valhalla GraphId), way_id, and live_speed_kph
### (null until enough probes have accumulated for that edge).
GET {{baseUrl}}/traffic/edge?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357

###

# ============================================================================
# /nearby  –  Explore nearby places (filter by category/group)
# ============================================================================

### Discovery: the filterable groups (food, health, shopping, …) and the
### precise category values in each. Use these to build filter chips.
GET {{baseUrl}}/nearby/categories

###

### All POIs within 1 km of Tahrir, blended distance+importance ranking (default
### sort=best). Admin boundaries / area "places" (Cairo, districts) are excluded.
### Each result carries distance_m. Second identical call returns X-Cache: HIT.
GET {{baseUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357

###

### Nearest-first (sort=distance) restaurants and cafes within 800 m.
### `category` is the precise OSM value; comma-separate or repeat the param.
GET {{baseUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=800&sort=distance&category=restaurant,cafe

###

### Filter by coarse group instead of exact type (all food places within 1.5 km).
GET {{baseUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=1500&group=food

###

### Pagination: page 2 of pharmacies within 5 km (limit/offset like /geocode).
GET {{baseUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=5000&category=pharmacy&limit=10&offset=10

###

### Scroll page 1 — take pagination.next_cursor from the response.
GET {{baseUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=5000&sort=distance&limit=10

###

### Scroll page 2 — offset-free, unbounded depth. Replace <CURSOR> with the
### next_cursor returned above (keep every other param identical).
GET {{baseUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=5000&sort=distance&limit=10&cursor=<CURSOR>

###

### Baseline route (no live traffic) – Tahrir → Giza. Note summary.time.
POST {{routeUrl}}/route
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

###

### Live-traffic route – same Tahrir → Giza, but opted into current traffic.
### date_time.type=0 (current) + speed_types including "current" make Valhalla
### use the live speeds written into traffic.tar. After posting the SLOW probes
### above, summary.time should rise vs. the baseline; after the free-flow probes
### (or once probes expire past TRAFFIC_EDGE_TTL) it returns to baseline.
POST {{routeUrl}}/route
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "costing_options": {
    "auto": { "speed_types": ["freeflow", "constrained", "predicted", "current"] }
  },
  "date_time": { "type": 0 },
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

